+++
title = "Journal 150726"

date = 2026-07-15

authors = ["aemshomy"]
+++


This is one of the few times when I am out of the spiral, where I decide that the best option is still ones my past selves have studied and understand. I think that throughout the various stages of growth in my life, I would face a major milestone or challenge, and from my perspective then, could not see past it, unsure about the future. However, even as I was unsure about the future, there were a few possiblities that I was happy with, there were more good paths branching outwards, paths that I would be satisfied to be on. The unknown is extremely destabilising, and uncertainty takes root during a spiral, leading to dysfunction and despair that remains in a feedback loop. But eventually, the loop would break, and I would be somehow convinced of doing something else for the time being, and distract myself with a productive activity. As time runs out, I unfortunately do not see much worth in what is left any much longer. The likelihood of something incredible happening and me turning my life around are statistically low, and I do not wish to continue much further. 

A futile expression nonetheless. I am a dead man walking, killed years ago by my own hand. I have lost any and all confidence in my ability to rebuild a semblance of a self anymore. When I was younger, I cameup with a multitude of tactics to manage my sanity. One of which was a council of 8 or 10 (I do not remember) split aspects of personalities that allow me to assume a set of traits that were beneficial at that point of time (logical/analytical, emotional, friendly, angry, jealous, etc). Over the years as social dynamics grew to become a larger part of my life, I have noted that between the ages of 14 - 17, my use of number 4 (the social one) greatly eclipsed the use of every other aspect of me. However, I think that during the latter part of my formative years, these pieces coalesced into a concrete single sense of self, and this self was mostly number 4, and bits and pieces of the other first few parts (analytical was number 3 or 5).

I think however, out of all the social skills that I have developed (and dulled over the years of disuse), a good balance of social sensitivity and risk-taking, some level of smoothening ability, a drop of playfulness and charm, a well of genuine interest, I have not yet developed a sense of trust. I do not trust anyone to treat me as I do treat them. I am used to being put in a disadvantageous situation, where someone has knowingly taken advantage of me (I enter these situations willingly, they are "testament" to my willingness to sacrifice myself, if they take advantage of me, I was right to distrust them, if not then great I have shown them I am a worthwhile friend). I win either way. I am confortable to be in this situation of disadvantage and misfortune, that I am not really upset at those who have betrayed me. Of course, there is some level of upset, and momentary anger, but at the same time, I deserved it for "trusting" them. It is definitely irrational. 

My time in France, has put me in a situation where all of the aforementioned social skills, are rendered useless. It is a time of complete disconnect with the people around me. Then, to my surprise, the disadvantageous situtions continued to occur, and now has fruitioned into an even more complete distrust of acquaintences, and who I am not close with. An issue that persists is that I am not incentivised to interact with people and / or sustain relationships. This is what will lead to eventual complete social isolation. This path seems more or less set in stone, and I do not see myself opening up anytime soon. I do not trust anyone anymore. 

The issue with complete social isolation, is that I there are very few situations where I can work under complete social isolation, and have enough money to sustain myself. And for that reason, I should just end it all. Nothing really has changed since I was 10, it just got worse, and I was betrayed by my own inability to commit. He thinks that I should have done it long ago. And is genuinely extremely surprised that it has not occured already. I don't really know what to say, as I am out of the spiral. I am out. I am lucid, there is no depressive mentality, anxiety, it's not even apathy - it signifies lack of emotion and feelings, but I am feeling strangely determined. I should end it, and the consequences don't matter, I am already dead.
